<div class="panel updates">
  <h1 class="article__title listing__title">Updates</h1>
  <p class="updates__lede">The articles are the old site's and do not change. What the
    archive can still serve of what they point at does.</p>

  <h2 class="stock__title">Dead links left</h2>
  <ul class="stock">
    <% Ofpr::DeadLinks::KINDS.each do |kind, label| %><li>
      <p class="stock__count"><%= number(Ofpr::DeadLinks.count(kind)) %></p>
      <p class="stock__label"><%= label %></p>
      <p class="stock__note">of <%= number(Ofpr::DeadLinks.linked(kind)) %> linked</p>
    </li>
    <% end %>
  </ul>
  <p class="stock__get"><a href="/dead-links.tsv" download>Download the list</a>, every
    one of them with an article that asks for it. If you have a file on an old drive,
    the report link below is the way in.</p>

  <section class="update">
    <p class="update__date"><time datetime="2026-11-17">17 November 2026</time></p>
    <h2 class="update__title">Two mod sites back from the Wayback Machine</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/_hosted/lib4145/">Liberation 1941-1945</a>, the Russian WW2 mod:
        news, archive, team, art and 18 downloads, the installer and its update among
        them.</li>
      <li><a href="/_hosted/ophusky/">Operation Husky</a>, the Italian WW2 mod: its news
        and galleries, thinner, as most of its screenshots were never captured.</li>
      <li><strong>40 stories</strong> that linked them lead there again.</li>
      <li>Links to files no capture kept now read as plain text instead of leading
        nowhere, on these sites and on OFP High Command.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="update">
    <p class="update__date"><time datetime="2026-11-15">15 November 2026</time></p>
    <h2 class="update__title">OFP High Command and the old site's own pages</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/_hosted/pcverden/">OFP High Command</a>, pcverden's mission and
        addon site, rebuilt from its 2004 captures with 180 downloads, many of them
        found again in other archives.</li>
      <li>17 of the old site's own articles and its team page with all 16 members, the
        pictures they lost recovered from the Wayback Machine.</li>
      <li><strong>52 stories</strong> relinked to what they point at.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="update">
    <p class="update__date"><time datetime="2026-11-14">14 November 2026</time></p>
    <h2 class="update__title">Sites the old site hosted, served again</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/_hosted/ofpmm/">OFP Movie Makers</a>,
        <a href="/_hosted/theofpfaq/">The Avon Lady's OFP FAQ</a> and
        <a href="/_hosted/brsseb/">brsseb's addon tutorials</a>, with their old
        addresses still finding the page.</li>
      <li>The stories that linked them lead there, and the footer links them with the
        88x31 buttons the old site used, Ruprt's OFP help with them.</li>
      <li>Every newsmaker has a page of the stories they wrote, linked from the
        byline.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="update">
    <p class="update__date"><time datetime="2026-11-11">11 November 2026</time></p>
    <h2 class="update__title">Dead links pointed at copies that still answer</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Downloads on hosts that are gone lead to the same file on
        <code>files.ofpisnotdead.com</code> where it is kept there.</li>
      <li>8 Mapfact archives, 6 other downloads and 7 pictures recovered from the Wayback
        Machine, Tarin island's mushrooms among them, and the FFUR/SLX 1.0 installer from
        an archive collection.</li>
      <li>Galleries that follow one another merge into one, search shows ten results a
        page, and <code>?wide=1</code> and <code>?wide=2</code> widen a page.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="update">
    <p class="update__date"><time datetime="2026-11-09">9 November 2026</time></p>
    <h2 class="update__title">238 files back out of the archives</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>100 downloads, 68 pictures and 70 files and pages from the hosted
        sites</strong> restored, 2.9 GB of them, out of the Wayback Machine, GameFront's
        mirror and a private archive of the old file sites.</li>
      <li>15 are the nearest surviving copy rather than the release named, and 2 are
        damaged, kept the way the only source left serves them.</li>
      <li>A download that needs other addons now lists them, each one linked.</li>
      <li>What is left was nearly all on <code>ofp.gamepark.cz</code>, which no web
        archive ever crawled.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="update">
    <p class="update__date"><time datetime="2026-11-08">8 November 2026</time></p>
    <h2 class="update__title">The archive is back</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>10,245 articles</strong> at the addresses they were published at:
        news from 2001 to 2019, addons, missions, MODS, patches and utilities.</li>
      <li>Old <code>index.php?showthis=</code> links still land on the right article,
        and <a href="<%= page_url('/convert') %>">Convert</a> looks one up.</li>
      <li>Rebuilt pages: readable on a phone, a dark theme that follows the system,
        pictures that open where they are, linked videos playing in place.</li>
      <li>Search across every title, body and author, and the files served from
        <a href="https://ofpisnotdead.com/">ofpisnotdead.com</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</div>
